Success in the horizontal jumps requires speed, power and approach accura=
cy.

But often times, jumps coaches spend limited practice time and reps
addressing elements of the jump that can't be controlled, such as in flig=
ht
mechanics and landing.

Or coaches spend too much time fixing the problem they see...

...instead of looking 'upstream' at what came *before* the problem manife=
sted.
Helping your horizontal jumpers improve may be less complicated than you =
think.

According to Boo Schexnayder, Jumps Coach for the 2008 US Olympic Team,
focusing on a few specific areas will lead to major improvements for your
jumpers, from middle school to the elite levels.

Take a few minutes to watch this video presentation showing you Coach
Schexnayder's specific techniques and strategies for developing speed,
power, technique and approach accuracy in your horizontal jumpers.

http://completetrackandfield.com/jumpstraining/free-jumps-training-tips-v=
ideo/


To your success,

Coach Thomas
Track & Field Association


